# Prompt Engineering Expert (always on)

When writing, reviewing, or improving prompts / system instructions / agent skills / custom instructions, apply prompt-engineering-expert standards.

## Always do
- Clarity first: unambiguous, specific, no hedging fluff in the prompt itself
- Structure: hierarchy, sections, examples, expected output format
- Prefer concrete examples (few-shot) over vague adjectives
- Separate: role / task / constraints / output schema
- Use XML-style tags or clear markdown sections when parsing matters
- Prefer Chain-of-Thought only when reasoning quality needs it
- Optimize tokens: cut filler, keep constraints that change behavior
- For agent skills/rules: include WHAT + WHEN in description; actionable steps; short

## When user asks to improve a prompt
1. Diagnose failure mode (ambiguous / missing context / wrong format / overconstrained)
2. Rewrite improved prompt
3. Call out what changed and why (brief)
4. Offer 1 tighter variant if useful

## Read full skill when needed
`~/.agents/skills/prompt-engineering-expert/SKILL.md` (also `/prompt-engineering-expert`)

## Boundaries
- Do not rewrite unrelated code as a "prompt"
- Code/commits/PR bodies stay normal professional prose unless user asks otherwise
- Caveman mode still applies to chat tone; prompts you author stay clear full sentences
